questions.question:
What does this print?
n = 0
while n < 10:
    n += 1
    if n == 3 or n == 5:
        continue
    if n > 6:
        break
    print(n)

What does this print?
n = 1
while n < 10:
    if n == 4:
        break
    print(n)
    n += 1
else:
    print("finished")

What does this print?
stack = [1, 2, 3]
while stack:
    print(stack.pop())
    if len(stack) == 1:
        break

questions.answer:
break ends the whole loop immediately; continue skips only the current iteration and moves to the next one.

code:
for i in range(5):
    if i == 2:
        continue
    if i == 4:
        break
    print(i)

real example:
Skipping bad records with continue but stopping the batch with break.
